				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				890,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize workspace file parsing into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `WorkspaceFileService.rs` into a dedicated submodule tree (`WorkspaceFileService/`) to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. Extract the main logic into `ParseWorkspaceFile`, the top-level JSON schema into `WorkspaceFile`, and the folder entry structure into `WorkspaceFolderEntry`.\n\nRename all internal types to strict PascalCase (e.g., `WorkspaceFile` → `WorkspaceFile::Struct`, `WorkspaceFolderEntry` → `WorkspaceFolderEntry::Struct`) and refactor the entry function to `ParseWorkspaceFile::Fn`. Integrate the existing `Cache::PathCanon::Canonicalize` utility for path resolution instead of raw `canonicalize` calls, ensuring consistency with the rest of the Mountain backend. Update `Source/Workspace/mod.rs` to reflect the new modular structure.\n\nThis structural refactor preserves all runtime behavior for parsing `.code-workspace` files while establishing a consistent namespace hierarchy for future workspace feature expansion.",
			"SHA": "5046a574af23f51fadbc60522f93bfdd952b1e28"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T00:43:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				886,
				20
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize cache layers into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose `AssetMemoryMap` and `PathCanon` from monolithic source files into dedicated submodule trees (`AssetMemoryMap/` and `PathCanon/`) to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention and improve modularity.\n\nExtract logical units (Entry, Map, Stats, LoadOrInsert, etc.) into separate files within their respective cache directories. Rename all public types and functions to strict PascalCase (e.g., `Entry` → `Entry::Struct`, `LoadOrInsert` → `LoadOrInsert::Fn`, `CacheStats` → `CacheStats::Struct`). Update `Binary/Build/Scheme.rs` and `Environment/Utility/PathSecurity.rs` to consume the new modular APIs.\n\nThis structural refactor preserves all runtime behavior (mmap asset serving, path canonicalization with moka eviction) while establishing a consistent namespace hierarchy for future cache expansion.",
			"SHA": "2a8ec534f8bd476cbf86dae0727b044f778bc569"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T00:08:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				868,
				2
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Coalesce tree-view emits and canonicalize webview payloads\n\nExtend the 16ms coalescing pattern to the `RegisterTreeViewProvider` RPC in `Source/RPC/CocoonService/TreeView.rs`. During extension boot, 30+ tree view registrations previously saturated the Tauri IPC channel. The new `TreeViewEmitBatch` singleton accumulates payloads and emits a single batch per frame, preserving the `sky://tree-view/create` channel while deferring to `sky-emit` logging for diagnostics.\n\nStandardize `webview` IPC payload shapes in `Source/Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest/Webview.rs`. Fix a critical bug where positional arguments (`[Handle, Value]`) from Cocoon were wrapped in `{ method, handle, args }`, causing SkyBridge's listeners (expecting `viewId` or `html` keys) to reject payloads, leaving iframes blank. The new logic detects wire formats, extracts named fields, and normalizes camelCase method names (e.g., `setHtml`) to kebab-case channel suffixes (`set-html`) to match the `Common` library definitions. Ensure both webview-panels and webview-views render correctly for extensions like Roo and claude-vscode.",
			"SHA": "6d8f8d296641459e47b373e39f865cfbe6b2219c"
		}
	],
